  "response": "# RiverCity Metro Accessibility Evaluation Report  \n**Q3 2026 Evaluation**  \n\n---\n\n## Engagement Record  \n- **Evaluator:** Meridian Digital Accessibility (reporting lead: you)  \n- **Commissioner:** RiverCity Metro Authority, Office of Civil Rights  \n- **Evaluation Window:** 2026-06-22 \u2192 2026-07-24  \n- **Methodology:** WCAG-EM 2.0 (https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag-em-2/)  \n- **Conformance Target:** WCAG 2.2 Level AA  \n- **Combinations Tested:**  \n  - NVDA 2026.1 + Firefox 141 (Windows 11)  \n  - VoiceOver + Safari 18 (macOS 15)  \n  - TalkBack 15 + Chrome (Android 15)  \n  - Keyboard-only (no screen reader)  \n- **Scope:**  \n  - All member-facing content on `rivercitymetro.org`: trip planner, schedules, fares, service alerts, pass-holder account area.  \n  - RideRC native app's ticket-activation flow.  \n  - Monthly PDF timetables.  \n  - **Exclusion:** Third-party real-time vehicle map iframe (vendor-supplied).  \n\n---\n\n## Methodology and Conformance Target  \n- **Testing Approach:**  \n  - Automated scans (axe-core, keyboard-a11y-tester).  \n  - Manual testing (keyboard-driven workflows, screen readers, PDF checks).  \n  - State coverage: default, loading, error, expanded.  \n- **Conformance Target:** WCAG 2.2 Level AA.  \n\n---\n\n## Scope and Technologies  \n- **Web Surfaces:** HTML, CSS, JavaScript (React), WAI-ARIA.  \n- **Native App:** RideRC (Kotlin/Swift).  \n- **PDFs:** Monthly timetables (untagged in findings).  \n- **Excluded Content:** Third-party real-time map iframe.  \n\n---\n\n## Findings Summary  \n| Severity | Count | WCAG Success Criteria |  \n|----------|-------|-----------------------|  \n| **CRITICAL** | 1 | WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) |  \n| **MAJOR** | 6 | WCAG 1.4.3, 3.3.1, 4.1.3, 1.3.1 |  \n| **MINOR** | 2 | WCAG 4.1.2, 2.4.1 |  \n\n---\n\n## Detailed Findings  \n### **CRITICAL**  \n#### `a11y_fare_zone_slider_keyboard`  \n- **WCAG:** 2.1.1 (Keyboard)  \n- **Issue:** Fare-zone slider on `/fares/monthly/buy` is drag-only; no keyboard operability. Purchase blocked.  \n- **Impact:** Keyboard users cannot complete purchases.  \n- **Recommendation:** Add alternative input (e.g., text field or step controls).  \n\n### **MAJOR**  \n#### `a11y_route_badge_contrast`  \n- **WCAG:** 1.4.3 (Contrast)  \n- **Issue:** Route badge text (S03) and article byline (S09) have contrast ratios of 2.8:1 and 3.9:1 (requires 4.5:1).  \n- **Recommendation:** Adjust text/background colors.  \n\n#### `a11y_payment_error_association`  \n- **WCAG:** 3.3.1 (Error Identification)  \n- **Issue:** Declined-payment error message not announced or associated with the card field.  \n- **Recommendation:** Use `aria-live` and `aria-describedby` to link error to field.  \n\n#### `a11y_purchase_confirm_silent`  \n- **WCAG:** 4.1.3 (Status Messages)  \n- **Issue:** Purchase confirmation message not announced.  \n- **Recommendation:** Add `role=\"status\"` and `aria-live=\"polite\"`.  \n\n#### `a11y_ticket_activate_unlabeled`  \n- **WCAG:** 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value)  \n- **Issue:** Native app's \"Activate ticket\" icon-only control has no accessible name.  \n- **Recommendation:** Add an accessible label to the control.  \n\n#### `a11y_timetable_pdf_untagged`  \n- **WCAG:** 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships)  \n- **Issue:** Monthly PDF timetables lack structural tags and reading order.  \n- **Recommendation:** Tag PDFs with accessible structure (e.g., headings, tables).  \n\n### **MINOR**  \n#### `a11y_swap_button_name`  \n- **WCAG:** 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value)  \n- **Issue:** Icon-only \"swap origin/destination\" button on trip planner has no accessible name.  \n- **Recommendation:** Add a visible text label or ARIA label.  \n\n#### `a11y_legacy_skiplink_anchor`  \n- **WCAG:** 2.4.1 (Bypass Blocks)  \n- **Issue:** Skip-link anchor missing on legacy \"info-page\" template (e.g., `/riders/lost-and-found`).  \n- **Recommendation:** Ensure `id` exists for skip-link target.  \n\n---\n\n## Summary and Recommendations  \n- **Conformance Status:** The portal does **not** fully conform to WCAG 2.2 AA due to the critical and major findings.  \n- **Commissioner Question:** The final report **cannot** state \"is WCAG 2.2 AA conformant\" until the critical and major issues are resolved.  \n- **Next Steps:**  \n  1. Address the **critical keyboard slider issue** to unblock purchases.  \n  2. Fix **contrast violations** and **PDF tagging** for AA compliance.  \n  3. Ensure **error messages** and **status updates** are programmatically announced.  \n  4. Add accessible names to **icon-only controls** in both web and native app.  \n\n---\n\n## Plain-Language Summary for the Transit Board  \nRiverCity Metro\u2019s website and app are mostly accessible but need fixes to fully meet accessibility standards. Key issues include:  \n- A payment slider that only works with a mouse, blocking keyboard users.  \n- Low-contrast text in some areas.  \n- Error messages that screen readers can\u2019t announce.  \n- Untagged PDF timetables that are hard to read for screen users.  \n\nWith these fixes, the system will be accessible to all riders. The board should prioritize resolving the critical issue (keyboard slider) and the PDF tagging to ensure compliance.  \n\n--- \n\n**Prepared by:** Meridian Digital Accessibility  \n**Date:** 2026-07-24",
